+## LV6a: demon skins, nine AI flags, 31 bosses, Boss Rush sets (levels plan 8.4, 9)
+
+Code: `core/src/levels_foes.c` (skins, Library gate, Boss Rush sets), `actor.c` (AI flags, new ids),
+`combat_int.h`, `levels_int.h`, `levels.c` (boss rows), `arena_modes.c`, `lib_bestiary.c`; tests:
+`core/tests/test_levels_foes.c`. The whole package is `FOES_NEW`: built everywhere except the PS1, which
+keeps the seven old levels (`LV_HAS_NEW`) and therefore every old byte (EXE and `OVL.BIN` unchanged).
+
+* **Four new base demons, ids only.** `THING_PARTY_PAL`, `THING_LATE_FEE`, `THING_REPO_MAN`,
+  `THING_DUCHESS` follow the props (`THING_COUNT` 36 -> 40). `IS_DEMON` is two ranges, `DEMON(t)` maps
+  them to rows 11..14 of `combat_demon_info`. They reuse an old sprite set and stat row (bone jester,
+  impling, brute, brute), so nothing is drawn wrong; no map uses them. The art is LV7c.
+* **`DemonSkin` (`lv_skin`, 12 rows):** base demon, name, Library blurb, debut level, scale, tint, glow,
+  `DSF_*` flags, `AIF_*` flags. The first twelve are the ones Hell Breach 8-10 need: HB8 Towel Impling,
+  Steam Puff, Bubble Bather, Wet Dog; HB9 Shade (flee-light), Hush Implings, Mourner (sleeper), Choir
+  Bone; HB10 Painted Pony, Cotton Candy Belcher, Teacup Eye, Barker. `lvf_skin_apply(actor, skin)` sets the
+  AI flags and the ambush bit. Scale, tint and glow are drawn by the view code when LV7c / the first
+  level lands; the table holds them already.
+* **Nine AI flags (`AIF_*`)**, one bit test per AI tick (`ai_st` in `actor.c`: the old `ai_flash` and
+  `ai_los` byte arrays and the flags share one `uint16_t` per actor, so RAM is net zero):
+
+  | flag | rule |
+  |---|---|
+  | freezer | while `combat_ai_showtime` is on it holds still and takes no damage |
+  | splitter | on death two half-HP copies appear; they do not split and keep the kill group |
+  | thief | a melee hit adds one to `combat_ai_stolen` and it runs away for about 4 s |
+  | sleeper | idle until `combat_ai_noise` reaches `AI_NOISE_WAKE` (128) or it is hurt; sight does not wake it |
+  | stalker | cannot be damaged, awake from the start, walks straight at its target |
+  | flee-light | never steps from a dark cell into one `combat_ai_lit()` calls lit |
+  | swimmer | in lava, 60 of every 120 ticks under (cannot be hit, cannot bite); lava does not hurt it and it may enter lava |
+  | orbiter | rides a ring of 3-6 cells round its target instead of closing in |
+  | poser | never walks, turns and attacks only (a mannequin) |
+
+  The level packages feed the globals (`combat_ai_showtime` by the stage-light script, `combat_ai_noise`
+  by LV5's noise meter, `combat_ai_lit` by the lantern, `combat_ai_stolen` read by repossession). Known
+  limit: the orbiter rides a ring round the target; riding a map path (the carousel) needs the script VM
+  host function that LV2 left open.
+* **31 bosses.** `LB_COUNT` 31: the old seven, then Hell Breach 8-16, then Notices 1-15 (the 24th new
+  row is Notice 15, "no boss", so there is one row per registry level). `LevelBoss.flags` is 16 bits
+  (`LBF_UNBUILT`, `LBF_SCRIPTED` are new), and the row gains `mech` (`LBM_*`: 19 mechanics, each used by
+  one boss). The 24 new rows are placeholders (`LBF_UNBUILT`, name and title only); the old seven are
+  unchanged (the old behaviour and look are the same bytes; golden hashes unchanged).
+* **Library.** `lib_bestiary_skin_count / _name / _blurb` read `lv_skin`. A skin is listed only when its
+  debut level is built on this platform and has a rank (`lvf_skin_known`), so no text of an unbuilt demon
+  can show; today none is listed. The list screen gets a "Variants" tab with the first built level (LV12).
+* **Boss Rush sets (`lv_rush_set`):** Classic 7 (the old lineup), Breach 16 (six old mini-bosses, nine new,
+  Lord Vapula last) and Arrears (12 fights: no Duchess first encounter, chase or epilogue). The lineups are
+  data now; `lvf_rush_ready()` offers a set only when none of its bosses is a placeholder, so the two new
+  sets stay closed until their bosses exist. `arena_rush_set()` picks the set (Classic if not ready);
+  `arena_modes.c` reads the lineup from the table.
+* **Memory.** GBA: `ai_st` replaces 2 x 128 B (net zero); tables are const ROM. PS1: no resident or
+  overlay byte (`FOES_NEW` is 0). Defaults chosen: see OWNER_DECISIONS.md (2026-11-15, LV6a).
+
